{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}GamerAI — a distributed AI compute network{% endblock %}
{% block extra_css %}
<style>
  .landing-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .6rem; margin: 1.25rem 0; }
  .hint { color: var(--muted); font-size: .9rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
</style>
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<div class="page">
  <h1>GamerAI</h1>
  <div class="muted" style="margin-bottom:1.25rem">
    A distributed AI compute network — members run a small agent on their
    own PC, and idle GPU/CPU time gets pooled into a shared job queue that
    serves chat requests across the network. Signing up and running the
    agent is how you join; there's no central inference bill because the
    compute comes from the members themselves.
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="landing-actions">
      <a class="btn" href="/demo">Try the demo</a>
      <a class="btn btn-quiet" href="/download/">Download the agent</a>
      <a class="btn btn-quiet" href="https://github.com/Hyrumdrums/GamerAI">View on GitHub</a>
    </div>
    <div class="muted">
      The demo needs no install — a rate-limited preview running on the
      network's smallest model. Download the agent to join the network for
      real: it walks you through creating an account on first run.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="hint">
    Already have an account? <a href="/login">Sign in</a>.
  </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
